# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
Narrator: Fire takes the Crooked Tree from root to crown, and high above the clouds, the leering grin on the moon twists into a bitter, prisoned scowl.
Narrator: In the hush that follows, Lord Phillip and Lady Adela draw close, smiling as their long sorrow finally scatters like ash upon the heather.
Narrator: You walk out of the Wytchwood together, living silhouettes breathing the cool, clean air of a valley set free from its oldest snare.
Narrator: Down in Wickermoor, the lanterns burn steady and gold, and the wind through the Oak of Many Faces sounds only like autumn leaves.
Narrator: At the platform, the Ghostlight Express waits with its brass lamps gleaming, ready to carry every one of you wherever your road leads next.
the_vagrant [smile]: Every ticket punched and accounted for, which is a rarer tune than my old fiddle usually gets to play.
if flag.last_ride_destination == "home"
Narrator: Ahead on the shining rails, the grey mist thins toward the warmth of morning and the waking world of the living you left behind.
endif
if flag.last_ride_destination == "province"
Narrator: The iron track curves outward toward another province of eternal night, where strange new lanterns wait beneath the quiet stars.
endif
if flag.last_ride_destination == "beyond"
Narrator: Beyond the edge of the valley, the Shroud parts like a velvet curtain, opening onto an uncharted world across the deep.
endif
Narrator: The whistle cries out clear and sweet, and the train carries you onward down the endless track.
-> END
